From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:01:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/40] function runner: share document allocation inputs with
 shadows

Matching database snapshots do not align IDs or creation times allocated by independent transactions. An insert followed by an index first/read records a cursor boundary containing those values, so equivalent executions can produce different read ranges even after by-ID insert normalization.

Capture the authoritative transaction's initial document generator and creation-time cursor before handler execution. Apply that state only to the non-committing verifier on the same snapshot, in both runtime directions and the paired mutation test path. Keep delayed V8 setup in the background and retain the initial state rather than the primary's advanced cursor. Ordinary transaction allocation and read-set comparison remain unchanged.

The database-only reproduction fails under independent allocation and passes with shared inputs; an extra verifier read still fails comparison. All 69 feature-enabled function-runner tests and 35 runnable isolate runtime acceptance tests pass, with three external-artifact tests explicitly ignored.
